)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Acetyl salicylic acid is an irreversible inhibitor of COX enzyme."},{"label":"B","text":"Acetylsalicylic acid reduces in vivo synthesis of prostaglandins."},{"label":"C","text":"Its clearance is independent of plasma concentration"},{"label":"D","text":"Antiplatelet effect of low dose aspirin is related to pre-systemic COX inhibition"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-48d776231a1e","stem":"Aspirin should be used with caution in the following groups of patients because of which of the following reason: (DPG-2011)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"In diabetics because it can cause hyperglycemia"},{"label":"B","text":"In children with viral disease, because of the risk of acute renal failure"},{"label":"C","text":"In gout, because it can increase serum uric acid"},{"label":"D","text":"In pregnancy, because of high risk of tera­to­genicity"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-85803f39b0d6","stem":"Aspirin inhibits which of the following enzymes?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Lipoprotein lipase (DPG 2009)"},{"label":"B","text":"Lipoxygenase"},{"label":"C","text":"Cyclooxygenase"},{"label":"D","text":"Phospholipase D"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5e3a5364f073","stem":"All of the following are correct statements except","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"PGs and leukotrienes are derived from arachidonic acid\b (AI 2001)"},{"label":"B","text":"Cox II is induced by cytokines at the site of in­ flammation"},{"label":"C","text":"Cox I is an inducible enzyme"},{"label":"D","text":"Leukotrienes cause smooth muscle contraction"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"bb958b685503bc5b334d54e049a58f8ce5513b70"},{"id":"q-9d7d98ee5b27","stem":"Which NSAID undergoes enterohepatic circulation?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Gastrointestinal","topicOriginal":"Gastrointestinal","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Phenylbutazone (AIIMS Nov 2006)"},{"label":"B","text":"Aspirin"},{"label":"C","text":"Ibuprofen"},{"label":"D","text":"Piroxicam"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Gastrointestinal","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-46bb479f5458","stem":"A 20 yr old female weighing 55kg is admitted to the emergency department having consumed 10 g of par- acetamol together with alcohol 6 hrs earlier. A serum paracetamol level is reported as 400 micro­grams/ml. Which of the following is correct with respect to this?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gastric lavage is mandatory\b (AIIMS Nov, 2004)"},{"label":"B","text":"Administration of activated charcoal"},{"label":"C","text":"Abnormalities of the kidney function are likely to be present"},{"label":"D","text":"Hepatotoxicity is likely to occur"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1bbaed0caf49","stem":"Prostaglandins have effects on a variety of tissues. The different prostaglandins may have different effects. Which of the following statements is not correct? (AIIMS Nov, 2002)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The human arteriolar smooth muscle is relaxed by PGE2 and PGI2 whereas TXA2 and PGF2α cause vasoconstriction"},{"label":"B","text":"PGE1 and PGI2 inhibit platelet aggregation 