allel and lateral to the ribs with hands inferior to the elbows and supinated."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Ribs","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"d4698f907eb0176d5f48389d406619587e02212b"},{"id":"q-f0b308475ed5","stem":"What structure separates the thoracic cavity from the abdominal cavity?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The mediastinum"},{"label":"B","text":"The diaphragm"},{"label":"C","text":"The peritoneum"},{"label":"D","text":"The pylorus"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Thoracic Wall and Mediastinum · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"6cd612883dd7e806a78dc35e70c9788793780ac2"},{"id":"q-fee3b0a5ae0a","stem":"Which structure within the cell produces ATP (adenosine triphosphate)?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the mitochondria"},{"label":"B","text":"the nucleus"},{"label":"C","text":"peripheral proteins"},{"label":"D","text":"the endopl