:false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review","repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"aa2c199c9923434fd555724b40822eba8870a8ce"},{"id":"q-0d637bef6378","stem":"The hypothalamus and core thermoreceptors notice if body temp too low. The hypothalamus signals smooth muscle in blood vessels to vasoconstrict and skeletal muscle to shiver. This activity causes body temp to rise, which is again noticed by hypothalamus & core thermoreceptors, so the hypothalamus turns 120 off these heat gain mechanisms. In this scenario, which of the following state- ments is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Neuroanatomy · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Neuroanatomy","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The scenario describes positive feedback in action."},{"label":"B","text":"The core thermoreceptors are the effector organs."},{"label":"C","text":"The hypothalamus is the control centre."},{"label":"D","text":"Skeletal muscle is the efferent pathway to the effector organ."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Neuroanatomy · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"e18d02c8db45c076074219aaf1f38fb51c5dfb04"},{"id":"q-4977f85f9df7","stem":"In homeostasis, what is it that produces the response that moves the physiologi- cal variable back towards the middle of its healthy range?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the effector"},{"label":"B","text":"the receptor"},{"label":"C","text":"the integrating centre"},{"label":"D","text":"the efferent pathway"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"1716e3f23ee8c9aec601bcab920396749238ef23"},{"id":"q-99ec7be9bf69","stem":"What does the word “homeostasis” refer to?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the steps leading to repair of a blood vessel and the coagulation of blood"},{"label":"B","text":"the maintenance of internal body conditions within narrow limits"},{"label":"C","text":"the controlled response that opposes the infl uence that caused it."},{"label":"D","text":"the production of blood cells in active bone marrow"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"16e731580c674bc791ef747be4708e4a3f142a08"},{"id":"q-088c7a3f81f7","stem":"How does homeostasis return the body to a healthy state after stressful stimuli? By producing a","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"responses that oppose the stress"},{"label":"B","text":"learned behaviour"},{"label":"C","text":"refl ex action"},{"label":"D","text":"buffering mechanism"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"2b60affd51f9ea0196078058d9823db17777f013"},{"id":"q-448051bb81e7","stem":"What causes the body to maintain a relatively constant internal environment?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"positive feedback"},{"label":"B","text":"homeostasis"},{"label":"C","text":"refl exes"},{"label":"D","text":"pH buffers"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"provisional_independently_reasoned","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"0e81fd107c734ce170aafdb980baaf64eb3d4305"},{"id":"q-6dbb3c041a70","stem":"Which of the following is a correct defi nition of “positive feedback”?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The process by which the body maintains homeostasis."},{"label":"B","text":"A mechanism in which the body’s response to a stimulus, opposes the stimulus."},{"label":"C","text":"A mechanism whereby the body responds to a stimulus by acting to enhance the stimulus."},{"label":"D","text":"The dynamic equilibrium maintained by an integrating centre which causes an effector to respond to the stimulus received by the receptor."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"51ac36a5ea95ae6d78744859639a9f6d3da9cff3"},{"id":"q-2b8aa640144d","stem":"Which of the following is a correct defi nition of “negative feedback”?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The process by which the body maintains homeostasis."},{"label":"B","text":"A mechanism in which the body’s response opposes the stimulus. 6 Homeostasis 123"},{"label":"C","text":"A mechanism whereby the body responds to a stimulus by acting to enhance the stimulus."},{"label":"D","text":"The dynamic equilibrium maintained by an integrating centre which causes an effector to respond to the stimulus received by the receptor."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"03ad38f927b32ddde6a3bb086af5086c880c9923"},{"id":"q-2324e2355275","stem":"What does the term “homeostasis” refer to?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"the chemical processes that take place in the organelles of the cells."},{"label":"B","text":"the body’s tendency to maintain a relatively constant internal environment."},{"label":"C","text":"the body’s use of energy to produce chemical substances and parts for growth."},{"label":"D","text":"any body response that opposes the stimulus that initiated the response."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"6ed4b49dd522069a36298ff472a22d2d3846cfd2"},{"id":"q-c8c24aefceb8","stem":"Which of the following would be a negative feedback response by the body to hyperthermia?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Shivering"},{"label":"B","text":"Sweating"},{"label":"C","text":"Vasoconstriction of blood vessels in the dermis"},{"label":"D","text":"An increase in metabolic rate"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"90b8479b35c2e83ae653bcc8e801e230b43659e6"},{"id":"q-45e4529161c1","stem":"How would the hypothalamus respond if its osmoreceptors noticed an increase in plasma osmotic pressure? It would send a message to","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Neuroanatomy · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Neuroanatomy","options":[{"label":"A","text":"the posterior pituitary to release more ADH"},{"label":"B","text":"the posterior pituitary to release less ADH"},{"label":"C","text":"the adrenal cortex to release less aldosterone"},{"label":"D","text":"the atria to release more ANP"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Neuroanatomy · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"exact_duplicate_projected_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","source answer/boilerplate removed from option D"],"duplicateStemGroup":"f672c3f26c34655adc8e08e8f88319e16ba82e63"},{"id":"q-f1b97805eebf","stem":"Which of the following statements about positive feedback and homeostasis is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are regulation 